  "id": "599fzgy",
  "title": "Chapter 12: Periodic Table",
  "order": 61,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2w1bbpq",
      "content": "The periodic table is the systematic arrangement of chemical elements based on their atomic numbers, electronic configuration and chemical properties. It is one of the most important tools in chemistry that helps scientists understand the relationships between different elements and predict their behavior."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Early Models",
          "value": "Triads & Octaves",
          "icon": "book"
        },
