          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pu05ogk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Periodic Trends"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fjtud4p",
      "content": "• Atomic size decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lcyd2b7",
      "content": "• Atomic size increases down a group."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c4fwp2l",
      "content": "• Metallic character decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bzcf0wz",
      "content": "• Electronegativity increases across a period."
    },
    {
      "id": "du83jn7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Importance of Periodic Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4gzaxwg",
      "content": "• Helps understand properties of elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently contrast Mendeleev's Periodic Table (atomic mass) with the Modern Periodic Table (atomic number).",
        "Pay special attention to Periodic Trends across periods and down groups in competitive exams.",
        "Identify the limitations of Dobereiner's Triads and Newlands' Law of Octaves."
      ],
      "id": "20xr3vc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "exx3wsu",
      "content": "• Predicts properties of undiscovered elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s7goh97",
      "content": "• Helps classify elements into groups."
    },
    {
      "id": "dhexcbf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rcxss39",
      "content": "• Mendeleev is called the Father of Periodic Table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0t4z40e",
      "content": "• Modern periodic table is based on atomic number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pdr45d3",
      "content": "• There are 7 periods and 18 groups."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sqficsg",
      "content": "• Noble gases belong to group 18."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
